Fig. 4. FER performance of BP decoding (red line), quantized NMS decoding                                V. CONCLUSION
(black line) and quantized NMS decoding with our post-processing (blue line)
for the (nb, mb, 384) NR LDPC with information length K = 3840.                  In this paper, a TS-based post-processing for quantized
                                                                              iterative decoder is proposed to lower the error ﬂoor of NR
     100                                                                      LDPC codes. The TS information for quantized decoding are
                                                                              collected by Monte-Carlo simulations and analyzed according
     10−1                                                                     to the BG structure. Our proposed post-processing will be
                                                                              performed when the ﬁrst-stage decoding fails. Two simple
     10−2                                                                     methods, CSCD and SA-CSCD, can be used in the post-
                                                                              processing. The provided simulation results show that our
     10−3                                                                     proposed scheme can efﬁciently lower the error ﬂoor of
                                                                              quantized decoders for NR LDPC codes.
